# Orbit Omni section QA (Europa lessons → forward)

Learned and locked on `006_Could-Life-Exist-Under-The-Ice-Of-Europa` Part 01 (approved rough `europa_part-01_rough_v03`). Apply to later Europa minutes and Omni-forward longs.

## Process

1. **~1 minute parts.** Write → script QA → VO + Omni for that part only → picture QA → approve → next part.
2. **Do not** generate the full episode in one pass. Regen only the failed minute / failed plates.
3. Prefer **Omni Flash** continuous journey takes + **native SFX** under Ben Orbit Narrator VO (this episode). Keep VO-literal picture.

## Motion coverage (no “broken video” freezes)

1. **Never freeze-pad** (`tpad` / last-frame clone) to stretch short Omni clips to VO length — it looks broken.
2. **Never loop / slow-mo** scenery (see `orbit-cutscene-no-reuse`).
3. Size inventory so **1× motion covers VO**: plan ~**8 unique ~8s Omni plates per ~60s** (or more). If short, **generate more unique plates** — do not pad.
4. Assembler must **fail** (or trim ≤~1s of VO) rather than freeze-extend picture.

## Picture quality bar (Part 01 lock)

1. **VO-literal journey** — Orbit doing the line (skim cracks while VO says scars; dive when VO goes under the ice).
2. **Gold beat to keep:** Orbit low over Europa linea + native Omni SFX while VO names cracks/scars.
3. **Europa surface:** pale cream-white ice + fine dark linea. Avoid large brown/red circular “pools” unless the beat is intentionally melt/chaos.
4. When VO enters the ocean / under the lid: **lean into the dive** (crack → plunge → subsurface ocean) — intentional water OK; muddy surface pools not.

## Single Orbit (hard)

1. **Exactly one Orbit** in frame at all times. Twin / clone / reflection duplicate = reject and regen.
2. Spot-check frames across each new plate (start / mid / end) before locking the rough.
3. Still attach canonical Orbit ref + identity lock on every Flow generate.

## Omni SFX joins

1. Hard concat of Omni beds makes the soundtrack **stop/jump** at every cut — feels like a break.
2. Assemble with **paired `xfade` + `acrossfade`** (~0.35–0.45s) so picture and Omni SFX blend across plate joins while staying A/V locked.
3. Keep Omni SFX under VO (typical ~0.2 volume); do not strip native beds unless QA asks.

## Prompt / gen hygiene

1. Prompts: continuous motion the whole clip; target ~8–10s; no freeze; single Orbit; VO-literal verb.
2. Run Flow Omni gens in a **durable foreground** session when background nohup dies mid-batch; skip-existing + per-plate retry.
3. Archive rejected plates (`_rejected_*`); bump asset version (`v02`/`v03`) rather than overwriting without a trail.

